course: dictionary
lesson: 3441
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The words around them are their context, and context tells you which meaning fits. The short word fa is a good example: it can be a music note, a football name, or slang.
explain: In music, fa is the fourth note of the scale: do, re, mi, fa, so, la, ti, do. In the song «Do-Re-Mi» from «The Sound of Music», children sing the notes, and «Fa, a long long way to run» is about that note. You can also spell it «fah».
explain: With capital letters, FA stands for the Football Association, which runs football in England, including the FA Cup. «In England the FA lets boys and girls play in mixed teams up to under-18.» Here the FA is a group of people, not a sound. Ask: does the sentence make sense with the music meaning? If not, try the football one.
explain: Slang can change a meaning completely. «Sweet FA» means nothing at all, as in «He did sweet FA all day.» It is a cheeky British phrase and is best avoided at school. When you meet fa, check the words around it before you choose a meaning.
fact: Fa is the fourth note of the musical scale.
fact: The sol-fa system uses the notes do, re, mi, fa, so, la, ti, do.
fact: Fa can also be spelt «fah».
fact: FA is short for the Football Association, which runs football in England.
fact: «Sweet FA» means nothing at all, and is best avoided at school.
exercise: In the song, children sing «do, re, mi, fa, so». Which note is fa? | The first note of the scale | A kind of football match | The seventh note of the scale | *The fourth note of the scale
exercise: «In England the FA lets boys and girls play in mixed teams.» What does FA stand for? | First Award | Fun Activity | *The Football Association | Fairy Adventure
exercise: «He did sweet FA all day.» What does sweet FA mean? | *Nothing at all | Lots of sweets | A football match | A kind of music
test: «The FA Cup is a famous English competition.» In this sentence, what does FA stand for? | *Football Association, because the FA Cup is a football competition | Flying Aeroplane | Fast Athletes | Football Association
test: Which spelling of the musical note is also correct? | fo | fu | *fah | fay
exam: In the words «Fa, a long long way to run», what does fa mean? | *A music note | A type of sweet | Nothing at all | Football Association
